      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! The wiki has exactly the answer you\u0027re looking for.\n\nAccording to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through the following mechanism:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n2. **The key is injected only into the environment of spawned child processes** \u2014 specifically the Ingest agent and Query agent \u2014 immediately before those processes start.\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** \u2014 it never holds the credential itself.\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential just by inspecting its own environment variables. The key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need to call the Anthropic API.",
